  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_geo",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "View-space normal (matcap space) and world normal / view direction (fresnel)."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_facet",
        "position": {
          "x": 526,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2292
        },
        "text": "`round(N × count) / count` snaps the normal to a coarse grid of directions; every grid cell is one flat facet. A small epsilon avoids a zero vector; *Facet Amount* blends from the smooth to the faceted normal."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_refl",
        "position": {
          "x": 3022,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "Matcap lookup with the faceted normal, weighted by fresnel `(1 − N·V)^power` so the reflection hugs the silhouette like a polished surface."
      },
      {
        "color": "#f472b6",
        "id": "note_inner",
        "position": {
          "x": 3022,
          "y": 681
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2990
        },
        "text": "Inner ray `d = normalize(lerp(I, −N, bend))` with `I = (0, 0, −1)` in view space. Red / green / blue use `bend × (1 − k)`, `bend`, `bend × (1 + k)` (k = dispersion), so the channels land on different matcap texels — the rainbow fringes of a real gem. One matcap fetch per channel."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_mix",
        "position": {
          "x": 6216,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "`emission = inner × gem colour × gain + reflection`. The albedo is a dark version of the gem colour so real scene lights still add a glossy specular highlight."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 6962,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Dark tinted base, very smooth, everything else is emission."
      }
    ],
